# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Without this file git stores whatever the working tree contains, so an editor
# configured for Windows line endings can commit CRLF into a repository that is
# otherwise LF throughout. That happened to chapter2.qmd, where the conversion
# rewrote all 1,285 lines and buried seven real edits in a whole-file diff.
#
# `text=auto` makes git normalise to LF in the repository for anything it
# detects as text. The `eol=lf` entries go further and keep LF in the working
# tree as well, on every platform, so an editor never sees CRLF to preserve.

* text=auto

# Prose and analysis sources
*.qmd  text eol=lf
*.Rmd  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Code
*.R    text eol=lf
*.r    text eol=lf
*.stan text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Data and bibliography. The CSVs are written by the analysis scripts and read
# back by read.csv, which accepts either ending; pinning LF keeps regenerated
# tables diffable line by line. None contains an embedded newline in a quoted
# field, so forcing the ending is safe.
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.bib  text eol=lf
*.csl  text eol=lf

# Configuration
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Binary: excluded from normalisation so text=auto can never mis-detect them.
*.png  binary
*.docx binary
